  },
  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Most people have heard the story of the lost city of Atlantis."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "But is any part of the story true?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "Over two thousand years ago, the Greek writer Plato wrote about Atlantis, an island in the Atlantic Ocean."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "The island’s people were very rich."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "They built a big city with many great buildings."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "But the people became greedy—they had many things, but they still wanted more."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "So the gods became angry."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "Earthquakes and large waves began to strike the island."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "Finally, Atlantis sank into the sea."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "Many explorers have looked for Atlantis."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "In 2004, explorer Robert Sarmast reported finding the remains of a city under the sea near Cyprus."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "However, Sarmast and other scientists later realized the structures he found under the sea were natural, not man-made."
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "Mark Adams, author of the 2016 book Meet Me in Atlantis believes the city was in Morocco."
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "Plato wrote about red and black stone circles around the city."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "Adams found similar red and black stones in the desert there, very near the Atlantic Ocean."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "Most people, however, think Atlantis is simply a story."
          },
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "The purpose of the story may be to teach people not to be greedy."
          },
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "Richard Ellis also wrote a book about Atlantis in 1999."
          },
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "He says “there is not a piece of solid evidence” for a real Atlantis."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "So was the island real or not?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "We only know one thing: The mystery of Atlantis will be with us for a long time."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
